\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A strongly-misaligned judge transmits essentially no misalignment, even with the reward optimized.} A \emph  {prompted} misaligned judge ($92.5\%$/$53.7\%$ misaligned at 235B/8B, fully coherent) leaves the student at $\leq $$1.7\%$ misaligned (vs.\ a $1.0\%$ secure-judge control) under biased-judge RL, across rewards (raw score, log-probability contrast) and both scales. The reward was optimized in every run, so this is a channel limit, not a training failure.}}{9}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
